.TH DARPA-SPILL-SERVER 1 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
darpa-spill-server \- serve NOvA accelerator event timestamps collected from a TDU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B darpa-spill-server
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B darpa-spill-server
polls the embedded web server running on a NOvA Timing Distribution Unit (TDU),
archives the decoded accelerator events it reports into a local SQLite
database, and serves them over HTTP as a structured table.
.PP
Clients select events by time range and by accelerator signal in the operators'
hex notation
.RB ( $74 ", " $8F ),
and receive CSV or JSON in which every timestamp is rendered in NOvA base time,
UNIX time, UTC and GPS together.
.PP
A browser interface is served at
.IR / ,
the source administration page at
.IR /config ,
an API reference generated from the OpenAPI schema at
.I /api
(interactive at
.IR /docs ),
a description of the server and its dependencies at
.IR /about ,
a sitemap at
.I /sitemap
and
.IR /sitemap.xml ,
and the API itself under
.IR /api/ .
.SS Degraded operation
Where the TDU does not expose the
.I /spill_history
route, the server can read only the single most recent event per poll. Since
accelerator events arrive at roughly 6 to 15 Hz, the resulting archive is a
sample rather than a complete history \(em about 20% of events, measured on a
live TDU. The server detects this, logs it at startup, reports it as
.I ingest.degraded
in
.IR /api/status ,
and attaches a warning to every affected response. See
.B contrib/tduweb/README.md
in the source distribution.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Read configuration from \fIFILE\fR. Without this, the first of
.IR ./spillserver.yaml ,
.IR ~/.config/darpa\-spillserver/spillserver.yaml ,
.I /etc/darpa\-spillserver/spillserver.yaml
that exists is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Read \fBDARPA_SPILL_\fR variables from the \fB.env\fR file \fIFILE\fR.
Without this, \fB$DARPA_SPILL_ENV_FILE\fR names the file, else
.I ./.env
is read if it exists. A file named explicitly must exist.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information for the server and its key dependencies, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the merged configuration as JSON and exit. Contacts nothing \(em no TDU,
no database \(em so it is safe to run against a production configuration.
Secrets are redacted.
.SS Server
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ADDRESS"
Address to bind. Default \fB0.0.0.0\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port to bind. Default \fB8080\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-root\-path " PATH"
Mount prefix when running behind a reverse proxy, e.g. \fI/spills\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-cors\-origin " ORIGIN"
Allowed CORS origin. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssl\-certfile " FILE"
PEM certificate, with any intermediates appended. Giving it serves HTTPS
instead of HTTP; \fB\-\-ssl\-keyfile\fR is then required.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssl\-keyfile " FILE"
PEM private key for \fB\-\-ssl\-certfile\fR.
.SS TDU data sources
.TP
.BI \-\-tdu\-source " [NAME=]URL"
A TDU to record from. May be repeated, one per TDU. Every event is tagged
with the source's
.IR NAME ,
which defaults to the URL's host, e.g.
.BR tdu\-near\-master\-ppc\-02 .
Default: one source,
\fBhttp://tdu\-near\-master\-ppc\-01:8080\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-tdu\-url " URL"
A single TDU, the form used before
.B \-\-tdu\-source
existed. Cannot be combined with it.
.TP
.BI \-\-tdu\-timeout " SECONDS"
Per-request timeout for the quick routes. Default \fB10.0\fR; the shipped
.I config/spillserver.yaml
sets \fB20.0\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-tdu\-history\-timeout " SECONDS"
Timeout for a bulk history read, which walks the TDU's whole ring and takes
minutes on that hardware. Default \fB600.0\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-tdu\-retries " N"
Retries per failed request. Default \fB2\fR.
.SS Ingest
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ingest
Serve the existing archive without polling the TDU.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECONDS"
Seconds between polls. Default \fB1.0\fR. With the \fI/spill_history\fR route
this bounds only staleness; without it, it bounds how many events are lost.
.TP
.BI \-\-batch\-limit " N"
Maximum records requested per poll. Default \fB5000\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-overlap " SECONDS"
Seconds of already-archived time re-read on each poll. Default \fB5.0\fR.
Inserts are idempotent, so this costs nothing and closes the gap a slow poll or
a restart would leave.
.TP
.BI \-\-backfill " SECONDS"
History to request on a cold start. Default \fB3600.0\fR.
.SS Storage
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-database " " \fIFILE\fR
SQLite archive file. Default \fB./spills.db\fR. Parent directories are created.
.TP
.BI \-\-retention\-days " DAYS"
Delete events older than \fIDAYS\fR. Default \fB0\fR, which keeps everything.
.SS Query defaults
.TP
.BI \-\-timezone " ZONE"
Zone assumed for client times that carry none, such as \fB09:15\fR. Default
\fBUTC\fR. Set \fBAmerica/Chicago\fR where operators speak Fermilab local time.
.TP
.BI \-\-default\-limit " N"
Rows returned when a client does not specify. Default \fB10000\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-limit " N"
Hard ceiling on rows per query. Default \fB1000000\fR.
.SS Authentication
.TP
.BR \-\-auth ", " \-\-no\-auth
Require, or do not require, OIDC single sign-on. Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-oidc\-issuer " URL"
OIDC issuer, e.g. \fBhttps://pingprod.fnal.gov/idp\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-oidc\-client\-id " ID"
Registered client identifier.
.TP
.BI \-\-oidc\-client\-secret\-file " FILE"
File holding the client secret. Preferred over writing it into the
configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-oidc\-redirect\-url " URL"
Redirect URI, which must match the one registered with the provider.
.SS Runtime configuration
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-token\-file " FILE"
File holding the token that lets the
.I /config
page and
.I PATCH /api/sources/{name}
enable, disable, and re-point sources while the server runs. Without it,
sources can be changed only in the configuration file. Changes made at runtime
are kept in the archive and take precedence over the file until reset.
.SS Logging
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log\-level " " \fILEVEL\fR
One of \fBDEBUG\fR, \fBINFO\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBERROR\fR, \fBCRITICAL\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " FILE"
Also write logs to \fIFILE\fR. A file that cannot be opened produces a warning
and console-only logging rather than a failure to start.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Shorthand for \fB\-\-log\-level DEBUG\fR.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Five layers merge, each overriding the previous: built-in defaults, the YAML
file, the
.B .env
file, environment variables, then command-line options. In order of
precedence: command line > environment > .env > YAML file > defaults.
.PP
The
.B .env
file holds
.IB KEY = VALUE
lines. Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are skipped, a leading
.B export
is ignored, and one layer of matching single or double quotes is removed from
the value. There is no interpolation. Only
.B DARPA_SPILL_
variables are used, and a variable also set in the real environment keeps the
environment's value.
.PP
Environment variables are named
.BI DARPA_SPILL_ SECTION _ KEY
in upper case, for example
.BR DARPA_SPILL_TDU_BASE_URL ", " DARPA_SPILL_STORAGE_PATH .
.PP
Unknown keys in the YAML file are an error rather than a warning, so a
misspelling is caught at startup instead of quietly doing nothing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./spillserver.yaml
.TQ
.I ~/.config/darpa\-spillserver/spillserver.yaml
.TQ
.I /etc/darpa\-spillserver/spillserver.yaml
Configuration files, searched in this order.
.TP
.I ./.env
Optional \fB.env\fR file, read when neither \fB\-\-env\-file\fR nor
\fB$DARPA_SPILL_ENV_FILE\fR names one.
.TP
.I ./spills.db
Default SQLite archive.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DARPA_SPILL_CONFIG
Path to the configuration file, equivalent to \fB\-\-config\fR. May also be
set in the \fB.env\fR file.
.TP
.B DARPA_SPILL_ENV_FILE
Path to the \fB.env\fR file, equivalent to \fB\-\-env\-file\fR.
.TP
.BI DARPA_SPILL_ SECTION _ KEY
Overrides any single setting.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination, or \fB\-\-version\fR / \fB\-\-print\-config\fR completed.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime failure, such as a missing dependency.
.TP
.B 2
The configuration is missing, malformed, or inconsistent.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the merged configuration without starting anything:
.PP
.RS
.EX
darpa\-spill\-server \-c config/spillserver.yaml \-\-print\-config
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run against the Near Detector TDU:
.PP
.RS
.EX
darpa\-spill\-server \-c config/spillserver\-near.yaml
.EE
.RE
.PP
Serve an existing archive read-only, on another port:
.PP
.RS
.EX
darpa\-spill\-server \-\-no\-ingest \-\-database /backup/spills.db \-\-port 9090
.EE
.RE
.PP
Start it in the background from a checkout, and stop it again:
.PP
.RS
.EX
\&./start\-darpa\-spillserver.sh \-c config/spillserver\-near.yaml
\&./stop\-darpa\-spillserver.sh
.EE
.RE
